1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,875
This man was trapped at the bottom

2
00:00:01,875 --> 00:00:03,600
of the ocean for almost three days.

3
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:04,680
And he survived.

4
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,326
In 2013, Harrison Okene

5
00:00:07,326 --> 00:00:08,720
was the cook on a tugboat,

6
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:10,760
off the coast of Nigeria.

7
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:12,890
Before dawn, in rough seas,

8
00:00:12,890 --> 00:00:13,800
the boat flipped over.

9
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:15,840
It sank upside down,

10
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,050
thirty meters to the seabed.

11
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,940
Harrison was in the toilet,

12
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:19,700
in his underwear,

13
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:21,250
as the water rushed in.

14
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,462
In total darkness, he felt

15
00:00:23,462 --> 00:00:24,910
his way through the flooded ship,

16
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:26,600
and found a pocket of air.

17
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,960
All he had was one bottle of Coke,

18
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,110
and two flashlights.

19
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:32,020
Both went dark within a day.

20
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:33,680
He could hear fish outside,

21
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:35,150
feeding on his crewmates.

22
00:00:35,450 --> 00:00:37,037
He prayed, as every breath

23
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,530
made the air more poisonous.

24
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:40,340
Sixty hours later,

25
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:42,590
divers came to recover the bodies.

26
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:44,590
One saw a hand, and reached for it.

27
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:46,210
The hand grabbed him back.

28
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:48,460
Of the twelve men on board,

29
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,180
he was the only survivor.

30
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,630
He swore he'd never go back to the sea.

31
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,310
Then he became a diver.
